Generic single-database configuration.

This directory contains the Alembic migration scripts for the application.

== Basic Usage ==

To create a new migration:

  alembic revision -m "create account table"

To apply migrations:

  alembic upgrade head

To revert migrations:

  alembic downgrade -1  # Revert the last migration
  alembic downgrade base # Revert all migrations

For more information, see the Alembic documentation:
https://alembic.sqlalchemy.org/en/latest/

== Configuration ==

The main configuration file is `alembic.ini` in the parent directory.
The `env.py` script in this directory is used to configure the database connection
and the target metadata for autogenerate.

The database URL is typically read from an environment variable (e.g., DATABASE_URL)
or directly from the `alembic.ini` file (though using environment variables is recommended for security).

Ensure your models are imported and their metadata is set in `env.py` for autogenerate to work correctly.
For example, if you have `Base = declarative_base()` in `app.db.base_class`, you would add:

```python
from app.db.base_class import Base
target_metadata = Base.metadata
```

And ensure all your models are imported so that `Base.metadata` is populated.
This might involve importing them in `app.db.base.py` or similar.
